---
description: Visual verification expectations for user-visible fixes
alwaysApply: true
---
When a fix changes user-visible behavior (panels, editors, Explore, generated queries shown in the UI):

Verify visually in addition to tests when feasible: capture a screenshot, a short recording, or both, showing the broken behavior and the fixed behavior.
Use what the repo provides: Playwright e2e (yarn e2e:playwright) records screenshots and video; a running instance (make run + yarn start) can be exercised with browser tooling.
Attach captures to the PR description and reference them from the ticket; name the exact page, query, or panel shown so a reviewer can reproduce it.
If visual verification is not feasible (pure logic change, or the affected UI path is not runnable in this tree), say so explicitly, rely on tests, and describe what a capture would show.
Never include credentials, tokens, or real user data in any capture.
